---
source: tests/stages.rs
expression: reports.report(path)
input_file: tests/fixtures/expand/doc_kernel_form_pages.knv
---
(def if-page "(if test then else)\n\nEvaluates `then` when the test is true, and `else` otherwise.\n\nIt emits a Rust `if` with an `else`.\n\n(if (> 2 1) \"yes\" \"no\")\n=> \"yes\"")
(def fn-page "(fn (parameter ...) body ...)\n\nMakes a function of its parameters, whose result is its last body form.\n\nIt emits a Rust `fn` item, a closure or a block, by where it appears.\n\n(local twice (fn (x) (* x 2)))\n(twice 3)\n=> 6")
(def match-page "(match value (pattern body ...) ...)\n\nEvaluates the body of the first arm whose pattern matches the value.\n\nAn arm's body is a `do`, so its last form is the arm's value.\n\nA pattern is `_`, a literal, a bare name, `(variant pattern ...)`,\n`(variant :field pattern ...)`, `(type-name pattern ...)` or\n`(type-name :field pattern ...)`. It emits a Rust `match`.\n\n(match 3\n  (0 \"zero\")\n  (_ \"other\"))\n=> \"other\"\n\n(match (pair 1 2)\n  ((pair left _) left))\n=> 1")
(def new-page "(new name (field value) ...)\n\nBuilds a struct value from its fields.\n\nA field label is a field name or a keyword, as in `(new car (:year 2025))`.\n`(new _ base (field value) ...)` takes the other fields from a base value.\n\n```\n(struct point (x i64) (y i64))\n(local start (new point (x 1) (y 2)))\n(field (new _ start (x 9)) x)\n=> 9\n```")
